1
00:00:12,178 --> 00:00:13,096
Ke?

2
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:16,266
Ke, it’s okay.

3
00:00:20,186 --> 00:00:21,938
Sam, this is so hard.

4
00:00:22,605 --> 00:00:24,482
This is just so hard.

5
00:00:25,108 --> 00:00:25,984
You’re disturbing Ke.

6
00:00:25,984 --> 00:00:27,277
Just go out first.

7
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:28,862
- She said you guys should go out.
- Just go out.

8
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:29,738
- Go out now.
- All of you.

9
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:30,989
- Hey.
- Are you hungry?

10
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:32,157
I’ll keep you company for now.

11
00:00:32,574 --> 00:00:33,533
Won’t you be late?

12
00:00:34,826 --> 00:00:35,952
No, it’s okay.

13
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:40,915
Lopez.

14
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:42,353
What’s up?

15
00:00:43,334 --> 00:00:44,711
I’ve been nice to you, right?

16
00:00:45,503 --> 00:00:46,504
Be nice to me.

17
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:48,006
Right?

18
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:48,965
Hey, Ke!

19
00:00:48,965 --> 00:00:49,799
Theo!

20
00:00:50,717 --> 00:00:52,093
Why are you alone?

21
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:53,678
Don’t you have a date?

22
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:55,305
A date?

23
00:00:55,889 --> 00:00:56,806
Should I have one?

24
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,142
Poor you.

25
00:00:59,142 --> 00:01:02,437
Fine, I’ll be your date tonight.

26
00:01:03,855 --> 00:01:05,982
Hello, is there anything you want?

27
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:07,525
What’s your order for today, ma’am?

28
00:01:07,525 --> 00:01:08,651
Sakura drink.

29
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:09,692
Okay.

30
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,907
Do you like anything else?

31
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:26,145
Ke.

32
00:01:27,727 --> 00:01:29,354
Stop caring, please.

33
00:01:32,634 --> 00:01:34,427
You know it’s not good for you.

34
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:39,557
Not good for me?

35
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:40,934
Not good for you?

36
00:01:49,692 --> 00:01:50,551
Kierra!

37
00:01:51,766 --> 00:01:52,767
Kierra, wait.

38
00:01:58,868 --> 00:01:59,911
I’m sorry.

39
00:02:01,871 --> 00:02:04,290
I don’t know what to say.
This is all new to me.

40
00:02:04,666 --> 00:02:06,251
You didn’t answer my question.

41
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:08,545
Not good for me or not good for you?

42
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:10,880
You don’t get it.

43
00:02:12,382 --> 00:02:13,925
I’m not the one deciding on this.

44
00:02:14,884 --> 00:02:16,386
What do you mean by “this”?

45
00:02:19,764 --> 00:02:21,266
Our relationship.

46
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:25,812
And what exactly is our relationship?

47
00:02:27,522 --> 00:02:28,648
I don’t know.

48
00:02:29,774 --> 00:02:30,817
You tell me.

49
00:02:32,277 --> 00:02:33,653
You have the upper hand, Ke.

50
00:02:34,028 --> 00:02:37,448
This is actually the first time
that I’m not in control of my feelings.

51
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:48,459
Maybe we got to
this point a little too fast.

52
00:02:49,627 --> 00:02:50,962
I don’t know you that well.

53
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:53,089
You don’t know me either.

54
00:02:54,097 --> 00:02:55,774
If you were to ask me...

55
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,736
maybe we should
start from the top?

56
00:03:02,483 --> 00:03:03,985
Start from the top?

57
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:07,270
Let’s start from the beginning.

58
00:03:08,855 --> 00:03:12,317
But we’ll only do it if we’re both ready.

59
00:03:31,502 --> 00:03:32,295
Hi.

60
00:03:34,422 --> 00:03:36,591
I’m Shan. Nice to meet you.

61
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:39,677
Hello! I’m Kierra.

62
00:03:43,264 --> 00:03:45,266
I’m hoping to get to know you more.

63
00:03:47,477 --> 00:03:48,811
I thought you were sick?

64
00:03:50,396 --> 00:03:51,397
I’m okay now.

65
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:33,124
If you want to tell me your story,
it’s better to start from the beginning.

66
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:38,921
But it’s up to you
how much you want to share.

67
00:05:50,116 --> 00:05:51,951
Julian Miguel Villaflor.

68
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:56,522
That’s his name.

69
00:05:58,858 --> 00:06:01,027
So, how did you two meet?

70
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:06,616
I’ll see you there.

71
00:06:06,949 --> 00:06:08,117
I’ll see you there, I’ll see you there.

72
00:06:22,334 --> 00:06:24,377
I really don’t wanna drink again.

73
00:06:25,643 --> 00:06:26,644
I’m done.

74
00:06:30,014 --> 00:06:31,099
Here you go, miss.

75
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:33,309
Thanks.

76
00:06:36,562 --> 00:06:38,898
You probably need this more than I do.

77
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:46,406
Still good, miss?

78
00:06:46,697 --> 00:06:47,740
Have another drink.

79
00:06:48,032 --> 00:06:49,367
I’m okay.

80
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:54,038
Do I know you?

81
00:06:54,622 --> 00:06:55,498
Just trying to help.

82
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:56,457
Huh?

83
00:06:56,457 --> 00:06:57,917
Help. I’m trying to help.

84
00:06:57,917 --> 00:07:00,378
What? Why are you yelling?

85
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:03,798
- I’m not yelling.
- I’m right next to you, and you’re yelling.

86
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:04,799
It hurts, you know.

87
00:07:04,799 --> 00:07:07,718
I’m not yelling. You’re the
loud one here, okay?

88
00:07:09,178 --> 00:07:10,221
What’s your...

89
00:07:10,763 --> 00:07:11,931
What’s your name and year?

90
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:14,183
Can’t you see?

91
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:19,772
Stop asking me questions,
you’re making me dizzy.

92
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:22,066
Okay. Okay, all right. I’m sorry—

93
00:07:22,525 --> 00:07:23,526
Kierra.

94
00:07:23,992 --> 00:07:24,951
I’m Miguel.

95
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:28,448
Julian Miguel Villaflor, and
apparently I’m your upperclassman.

96
00:07:28,698 --> 00:07:29,699
I’m ahead of you.

97
00:07:30,533 --> 00:07:31,256
Who?

98
00:07:32,243 --> 00:07:32,850
Huh?

99
00:07:33,286 --> 00:07:34,370
Who’s asking?

100
00:07:37,331 --> 00:07:37,999
Wait.

101
00:07:39,625 --> 00:07:40,793
Villaflor?

102
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:41,836
Villaflor.

103
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:44,213
You’re famous.

104
00:07:44,213 --> 00:07:44,922
Hmm.

105
00:07:44,922 --> 00:07:47,633
Nice to meet you, Mayor.

106
00:07:49,218 --> 00:07:49,927
Villaflor.

107
00:07:51,129 --> 00:07:52,047
Nice to meet you.

108
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:55,141
But that’s not me, that’s my dad.

109
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:59,645
I’m just Miguel Villaflor, not the Mayor.

110
00:08:00,021 --> 00:08:00,563
Yup.

111
00:08:01,545 --> 00:08:02,421
You still look just like him.

112
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:04,442
You’re the son of a crook.

113
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,655
- Okay, all right.
- A crook.

114
00:08:10,990 --> 00:08:13,826
Can you manage?
It’s quite dirty if you fall.

115
00:08:13,826 --> 00:08:14,744
What? Okay—

116
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:16,162
I can handle myself.

117
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:16,846
Yeah?

118
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:17,830
I’m pretty strong.

119
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:18,289
Strong?

120
00:08:18,289 --> 00:08:19,582
Strong!

121
00:08:19,707 --> 00:08:20,500
Okay.

122
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:22,668
Okay. I believe you.

123
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:24,962
I believe you’re strong,
but I have a car.

124
00:08:24,962 --> 00:08:26,839
I can take you home,
wherever you are.

125
00:08:27,256 --> 00:08:28,295
Do you want that?

126
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:29,634
I can manage, Mayor.

127
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:31,636
I don’t really believe you.

128
00:08:32,428 --> 00:08:33,054
Ke?

129
00:08:33,054 --> 00:08:34,263
- I can manage.
- Okay, all right.

130
00:08:34,586 --> 00:08:35,796
I don’t believe you one bit.

131
00:08:36,182 --> 00:08:36,599
Ke?

132
00:08:36,849 --> 00:08:38,476
- Oh.
- Theo!

133
00:08:38,476 --> 00:08:41,562
Bro, sorry. You can
see she can barely stand.

134
00:08:41,562 --> 00:08:42,647
Do you know her?

135
00:08:42,897 --> 00:08:44,732
I was going to help her.
I was going to take her home.

136
00:08:45,441 --> 00:08:46,817
Yeah, yeah. She’s my friend.

137
00:08:47,534 --> 00:08:48,827
I’ve got it, bro. Thank you.

138
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:51,030
No problem. It’s okay.

139
00:08:51,397 --> 00:08:52,940
Nice to meet you, ma’am.

140
00:08:57,036 --> 00:09:00,039
You keep popping up out of nowhere.

141
00:09:00,164 --> 00:09:02,166
Duh, we’re in the same school.

142
00:09:02,291 --> 00:09:03,125
Hey!

143
00:09:03,626 --> 00:09:05,169
Wait, where are your friends?

144
00:09:07,296 --> 00:09:09,781
Luna’s with Kalix.

145
00:09:10,883 --> 00:09:12,843
Via already got picked up by Arkin.

146
00:09:14,804 --> 00:09:17,431
Yanna went somewhere.

147
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:21,519
Sam… I don’t know where she went.

148
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:24,391
- Sevi said, he said—
- Okay. Yup.

149
00:09:25,314 --> 00:09:26,524
It’s okay. I get it.

150
00:09:27,024 --> 00:09:29,986
Let’s just go home, okay?
I’ll walk you back.

151
00:09:30,653 --> 00:09:32,196
- Hold on.
- Let’s go, let’s go.

152
00:09:32,196 --> 00:09:33,197
- Let’s go.
- Wait.

153
00:09:33,531 --> 00:09:37,118
Why is everyone around me taken?

154
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:40,663
When will it be my turn?

155
00:09:42,388 --> 00:09:44,307
What’s it even like to have a boyfriend?

156
00:09:47,545 --> 00:09:50,006
When will someone finally like me?

157
00:09:53,217 --> 00:09:56,596
Because when I have a boyfriend—

158
00:09:59,932 --> 00:10:01,475
- screw all of you.
- Hey.

159
00:10:04,095 --> 00:10:04,984
Okay.

160
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:06,772
It’ll happen someday.

161
00:10:07,898 --> 00:10:10,401
For now, come on.

162
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:12,981
I’ll take you home,
because I’d be in

163
00:10:13,005 --> 00:10:15,590
trouble with Master if
I left you here drunk.

164
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:17,033
Okay, carry me.

165
00:10:17,158 --> 00:10:17,908
Huh? No.

166
00:10:17,908 --> 00:10:18,993
- Come on.
- No.

167
00:10:19,577 --> 00:10:20,281
Huh.

168
00:10:20,807 --> 00:10:21,933
Oh my god!

169
00:10:22,204 --> 00:10:23,080
Let’s go here.

170
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:25,291
No. That’s not your house.

171
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:27,835
Huh? No, that’s where I came from…

172
00:10:30,908 --> 00:10:33,911
I told Theo about it.

173
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:37,511
Because I always wanted to be loved.

174
00:10:39,221 --> 00:10:44,644
I was overflowing with love
from childhood until I grew up.

175
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:49,031
But the kind of love
I’m looking for now is different.

176
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:56,739
It’s no longer just from family or friends.

177
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:02,891
I want to spend my whole life with someone.

178
00:11:05,122 --> 00:11:11,712
Someone I can be with until we’re old.

179
00:11:16,967 --> 00:11:18,094
Sorry, Doc.

180
00:11:19,428 --> 00:11:20,429
I didn’t finish the story.

181
00:11:21,706 --> 00:11:24,084
Where did I stop?

182
00:11:24,684 --> 00:11:27,186
You can continue
from after the day you first met.

183
00:11:28,771 --> 00:11:29,897
The next day...

184
00:11:31,816 --> 00:11:34,110
<i>While I was walking through school.</i>

185
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:40,133
Kierra?

186
00:11:42,115 --> 00:11:42,961
Hi.

187
00:11:44,790 --> 00:11:46,008
How are you?

188
00:11:48,708 --> 00:11:50,334
You don’t remember me.

189
00:11:50,334 --> 00:11:51,752
Uhm, Miguel.

190
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:55,840
Julian Miguel Villaflor, reintroduction.

191
00:11:57,717 --> 00:11:58,718
Last night.

192
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:02,555
You were so out of it.
You were drunk.

193
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:05,408
Villaflor?

194
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:06,183
Villaflor.

195
00:12:06,726 --> 00:12:09,687
Ah, the loud one from last night.

196
00:12:10,101 --> 00:12:10,977
The Mayor’s son?

197
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,982
You don’t have to say it like that.

198
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:16,527
How are you? Still hungover?

199
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:18,404
Is that why you’re having ice cream?

200
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:20,364
Yeah, my head still hurts a bit.

201
00:12:20,364 --> 00:12:22,283
Mhmm. I can imagine.

202
00:12:23,325 --> 00:12:25,202
I can imagine because—

203
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:28,414
You’re not supposed to drink
when you have class the next day.

204
00:12:29,373 --> 00:12:30,164
Right?

205
00:12:34,086 --> 00:12:35,713
Okay, I’m gonna go ahead. I’ll be late.

206
00:12:36,046 --> 00:12:36,860
No, wait.

207
00:12:37,757 --> 00:12:38,382
Sorry.

208
00:12:39,437 --> 00:12:40,188
Sorry.

209
00:12:42,762 --> 00:12:44,086
Can I get your socials?

210
00:12:46,932 --> 00:12:47,600
Please?

211
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:50,110
Okay.

212
00:13:01,071 --> 00:13:02,031
You owe me a reply, okay.

213
00:13:45,157 --> 00:13:48,160
<i>Hello, Mayor’s son.</i>

214
00:13:48,786 --> 00:13:52,206
<i>Hi, future girlfriend of the mayor’s son.</i>

215
00:13:52,373 --> 00:13:53,666
<i>Butterflies.</i>

216
00:13:54,375 --> 00:13:56,418
<i>That’s what I felt that night.</i>

217
00:13:56,961 --> 00:14:00,130
<i>Since then, we’ve been</i>
<i>meeting up to eat together.</i>

218
00:14:04,176 --> 00:14:08,305
<i>Who’s that guy with you in your post?</i>

219
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:09,932
<i>He’s Sevi.</i>

220
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:12,059
<i>We’ve been friends since high school.</i>

221
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:14,019
<i>Are you jealous?</i>

222
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:17,305
<i>Sorry.</i>

223
00:14:17,857 --> 00:14:20,818
<i>I just don’t feel comfortable with</i>
<i>guys coming over to your condo. </i>

224
00:14:22,194 --> 00:14:24,321
<i>Can you keep your</i>
<i>distance from him?</i>

225
00:14:26,519 --> 00:14:28,641
<i>You’re so cute when you’re jealous.</i>

226
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:35,457
<i>I thought his jealousy was just</i>
<i>him showing he was really into me.</i>

227
00:14:36,041 --> 00:14:39,461
<i>I didn’t realize that it
was something else.</i>

228
00:14:44,174 --> 00:14:47,094
Wait. You’re saying five...
ten more minutes?

229
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:48,387
Didn’t you say that a while ago?

230
00:14:48,768 --> 00:14:50,061
I placed an advance order.

231
00:14:50,347 --> 00:14:51,765
Why can’t you serve it all at once?

232
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:53,274
What use are you then?

233
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:55,603
Sorry, sir. I’ll follow up.

234
00:14:55,769 --> 00:14:58,063
Following up again?
You already said that earlier.

235
00:14:58,063 --> 00:14:58,856
Your menu is so expensive.

236
00:14:58,856 --> 00:14:59,748
What are you going to
do? That’s the service…

237
00:14:59,772 --> 00:15:00,274
No, wait. It’s okay.

238
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:01,817
- Your service is so expensive.
- Miguel. Miguel, it’s okay.

239
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:02,735
No, what’s your plan?

240
00:15:02,735 --> 00:15:03,903
- We paid good money for—
- It’s okay.

241
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:05,070
- Your menu is really expensive.
- It’s okay, Miguel.

242
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:06,610
Miguel… It’s okay.

243
00:15:07,156 --> 00:15:08,449
I’m still full, anyway.

244
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:11,785
Sorry. Can you just
serve it once it’s ready?

245
00:15:12,286 --> 00:15:13,579
I’m really sorry.

246
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:14,288
It’s okay.

247
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:16,040
I can’t believe it.

248
00:15:16,165 --> 00:15:17,291
Motherfucker.

249
00:15:19,585 --> 00:15:20,169
Sorry.

250
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:21,170
I’m sorry, okay?

251
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:23,130
The restaurant is so expensive.

252
00:15:23,401 --> 00:15:25,055
We’re supposed to be
paying for their service,

253
00:15:25,079 --> 00:15:26,696
so if this is what
their service is like...

254
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:28,177
You understand how it would—

255
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:30,638
mess me up.

256
00:15:31,722 --> 00:15:33,974
But, cheers to you.

257
00:15:35,309 --> 00:15:37,686
Thank you for coming with me.

258
00:15:43,108 --> 00:15:43,817
Not bad.

259
00:15:44,318 --> 00:15:45,402
Okay, so...

260
00:15:46,570 --> 00:15:49,531
Tell me about your ex.

261
00:15:49,865 --> 00:15:51,575
Exes? Is that right?

262
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:53,535
No. I don’t have any exes.

263
00:15:53,911 --> 00:15:54,787
No.

264
00:15:55,329 --> 00:15:55,955
I don’t.

265
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:58,082
No, you don’t have to be modest.

266
00:15:58,082 --> 00:15:59,792
- Just be honest.
- I don’t, I don’t have any.

267
00:15:59,792 --> 00:16:01,627
So I don’t have anything to tell you.

268
00:16:01,835 --> 00:16:02,670
What about you?

269
00:16:03,879 --> 00:16:05,297
How many exes have you had?

270
00:16:05,631 --> 00:16:07,925
I had...

271
00:16:08,592 --> 00:16:11,929
I had three.

272
00:16:12,471 --> 00:16:17,810
But two of them weren’t that serious,
it was more like just playing around.

273
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:21,647
But the other one, it got a bit serious—

274
00:16:23,478 --> 00:16:27,065
Unfortunately, she cheated on me. So, I...

275
00:16:28,195 --> 00:16:30,406
Well, she decided to break up.

276
00:16:31,615 --> 00:16:32,436
Really?

277
00:16:33,283 --> 00:16:34,243
Yeah, yeah.

278
00:16:35,744 --> 00:16:40,916
But because of that, I developed
trust issues and insecurity.

279
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:43,252
I don’t really want to blame her for that.

280
00:16:44,081 --> 00:16:47,334
And I wanted to get back
together, fix the relationship.

281
00:16:48,132 --> 00:16:52,011
But she didn't want to anymore,
so we just had to break up.

282
00:16:53,775 --> 00:16:55,485
I’m so sorry that happened to you.

283
00:16:56,348 --> 00:16:57,092
Yeah.

284
00:17:00,686 --> 00:17:01,937
Have you moved on?

285
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:02,980
Yeah.

286
00:17:03,188 --> 00:17:04,023
Of course.

287
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:06,442
Very fast, ‘cause she’s not that pretty.

288
00:17:09,478 --> 00:17:16,360
But she had the gall to go around
everywhere saying that it’s my fault.

289
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:17,661
What?

290
00:17:17,661 --> 00:17:19,872
Right? Yeah. I know. Same reaction.

291
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:22,624
It’s my fault, apparently.
I’m the one who cheated.

292
00:17:22,958 --> 00:17:25,878
And so just imagine
the shock I felt, right?

293
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:28,756
I wanted to be the bigger man.

294
00:17:29,256 --> 00:17:30,065
Right.

295
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:31,266
Be a gentleman about it.

296
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:33,135
Because I loved her.

297
00:17:33,761 --> 00:17:35,763
Just let her do whatever she wants,

298
00:17:35,971 --> 00:17:40,601
because at the end of the day, if I didn’t
do it, why should I have to defend myself?

299
00:17:41,643 --> 00:17:46,732
Of course. But you should still
defend yourself when it’s not true.

300
00:17:46,982 --> 00:17:50,402
Otherwise, that’s what other
people might end up thinking of you.

301
00:17:57,242 --> 00:17:58,133
Wow.

302
00:17:58,827 --> 00:18:02,039
You know what, Kierra, you
remind me so much of my mom.

303
00:18:02,873 --> 00:18:03,957
Do you know what she told me?

304
00:18:04,833 --> 00:18:10,214
She told me that, “More than anyone,
you have to know yourself better.”

305
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:12,299
“You know yourself best.”

306
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:18,347
So I like to believe she’s
up there in heaven, still believing me.

307
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:22,976
I’m so sorry. What happened?

308
00:18:22,976 --> 00:18:24,269
If you don’t mind me asking.

309
00:18:24,269 --> 00:18:26,188
No, no. I don’t mind. It’s you.

310
00:18:26,939 --> 00:18:32,319
Well, basically she was
gone by my second grade.

311
00:18:33,096 --> 00:18:37,975
So now it’s just me, my dad, and—

312
00:18:38,951 --> 00:18:39,618
you.

313
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:49,461
<i>He had a lot of tragic stories, and—</i>

314
00:18:50,295 --> 00:18:52,089
I empathized with him a lot.

315
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:59,138
I wish I had gotten to know him fully
before we got into a relationship.

316
00:19:00,347 --> 00:19:08,689
At first, I guess I was blinded
by everything he was doing.

317
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:10,149
Everything he was showing me.

318
00:19:10,149 --> 00:19:12,276
<i>He was nice.</i>

319
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:15,529
<i>He was thoughtful.</i>

320
00:19:16,113 --> 00:19:18,031
<i>Caring in his own way.</i>

321
00:19:19,366 --> 00:19:26,206
But I found out too late that he was just—

322
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:35,007
really manipulative and
would lie about a lot of things.

323
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:36,884
Hey, I didn’t do it.

324
00:19:37,509 --> 00:19:38,719
I promise, I didn’t do it.

325
00:19:39,344 --> 00:19:40,137
Hey, it really wasn’t me.

326
00:19:40,137 --> 00:19:41,555
- Who was it?
- Believe me.

327
00:19:44,016 --> 00:19:45,184
They came on to me.

328
00:19:45,517 --> 00:19:46,143
They?

329
00:19:46,518 --> 00:19:47,644
She came on to me.

330
00:19:47,728 --> 00:19:49,938
Okay, I slipped.
How was I supposed to know?

331
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:52,441
Maybe they go by they/them.
How would I know?

332
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:53,525
Do you understand?

333
00:19:53,734 --> 00:19:58,780
It just so happened that she
was at the same place as me.

334
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:03,702
We were talking, and then she kept
going on about how much she wanted me...

335
00:20:04,036 --> 00:20:04,661
And?

336
00:20:04,995 --> 00:20:06,038
Nothing happened.

337
00:20:06,705 --> 00:20:07,998
I promise you nothing happened.

338
00:20:08,665 --> 00:20:09,895
You believe me?

339
00:20:10,292 --> 00:20:10,851
Right?

340
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:12,002
I wouldn’t lie to you.

341
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:14,004
I wouldn’t lie to you.

342
00:20:14,546 --> 00:20:15,839
Nothing happened.

343
00:20:16,256 --> 00:20:17,090
I promise you.

344
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:20,761
I promise you.
I’m not lying to you.

345
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:21,595
Okay.

346
00:20:22,387 --> 00:20:24,223
Kierra, you’re the only one.

347
00:20:25,515 --> 00:20:31,480
<i>And I just believed him,</i>
<i>because I really loved him.</i>

348
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:35,692
So much.

349
00:20:38,544 --> 00:20:40,963
I’m angry that I loved him.

350
00:20:43,016 --> 00:20:47,813
Because there’s...
there’s nothing left of me.

351
00:20:50,457 --> 00:20:51,625
I knew—

352
00:20:51,917 --> 00:20:58,423
I knew everyone around
me would probably be so upset…

353
00:21:00,008 --> 00:21:00,981
with what—

354
00:21:02,742 --> 00:21:04,202
I was doing.

355
00:21:06,974 --> 00:21:09,017
I didn’t think about it anymore.

356
00:21:09,851 --> 00:21:12,062
I was just too scared of him.

357
00:21:13,063 --> 00:21:17,401
I was scared to leave whatever we had.

358
00:21:20,195 --> 00:21:22,114
I should have known better.

359
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:24,866
No, Kierra.

360
00:21:25,617 --> 00:21:27,703
You couldn’t have known.

361
00:21:29,454 --> 00:21:34,501
Because you loved the man
that he showed you at the start.

362
00:21:34,918 --> 00:21:37,504
And he chose not to let you know.

363
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:49,224
Sometimes I wonder if he was
like that with his exes, too.

364
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:51,977
If he treated them like real people.

365
00:21:53,061 --> 00:21:55,647
Because he didn’t treat me like one.

366
00:21:57,858 --> 00:22:00,444
He never treated me like a person.

367
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:07,159
I was just like a thing that he could just—

368
00:22:10,579 --> 00:22:12,956
Did he lie about other things?

369
00:22:14,833 --> 00:22:16,960
He also lied about his mom.

370
00:22:18,962 --> 00:22:21,048
His mom is still alive.

371
00:22:25,886 --> 00:22:28,430
He cheated on his exes too.

372
00:22:31,016 --> 00:22:34,311
And he cheated on me too.

373
00:22:36,063 --> 00:22:37,439
How many times?

374
00:22:37,939 --> 00:22:39,399
Multiple times.

375
00:22:42,319 --> 00:22:52,496
I found out he cheated on me the
same time he hurt me for the first time.

376
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:55,374
Fuck, Kierra. I already told you.

377
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:57,751
I already told you!

378
00:22:58,085 --> 00:22:59,419
You’re not listening.

379
00:22:59,711 --> 00:23:00,921
I already told you, didn’t I?

380
00:23:00,921 --> 00:23:02,130
Didn’t I just tell you a minute ago?

381
00:23:02,130 --> 00:23:03,340
Why aren’t you listening, huh?

382
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:04,174
Answer me.

383
00:23:04,758 --> 00:23:05,258
Answer!

384
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:08,053
Look at me, look at me.

385
00:23:08,261 --> 00:23:09,054
Answer.

386
00:23:09,388 --> 00:23:10,389
Answer me.

387
00:23:10,597 --> 00:23:11,765
- Fucking answer!
- Yes.

388
00:23:13,016 --> 00:23:15,102
One more. One more time.

389
00:23:15,519 --> 00:23:17,145
I’ll let you realize.

390
00:23:17,521 --> 00:23:20,899
I’m sorry. I can’t go on.

391
00:23:21,608 --> 00:23:25,362
No, it’s okay. You’ve done
enough already, Kierra.

392
00:23:26,405 --> 00:23:31,410
And again, do not apologize
for taking things slow.

393
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:33,995
And for being patient with yourself.

394
00:23:33,995 --> 00:23:36,498
It’s okay. You’ve done great.

395
00:23:37,416 --> 00:23:39,126
We can end the session here.

396
00:24:03,733 --> 00:24:05,068
Are you okay?

397
00:24:09,197 --> 00:24:10,157
Hey.

398
00:24:12,784 --> 00:24:14,077
Why?

399
00:24:14,536 --> 00:24:15,954
Did something happen?

400
00:24:21,168 --> 00:24:22,502
Is something wrong?

401
00:24:24,379 --> 00:24:26,965
Thank you for staying by my side.

402
00:24:28,967 --> 00:24:30,677
What’s this about?

403
00:24:31,636 --> 00:24:33,763
I went back to therapy.

404
00:24:37,934 --> 00:24:39,478
How was it?

405
00:24:40,961 --> 00:24:45,329
It’s hard to retell what
happened,

406
00:24:45,393 --> 00:24:49,761
because it feels like I’m going
through all of it again.

407
00:24:52,881 --> 00:24:54,716
But I’m trying.

408
00:24:57,746 --> 00:25:02,417
I want the happy Kierra to come back.

409
00:25:07,547 --> 00:25:09,883
I’m so proud of you, Ke.

410
00:25:11,968 --> 00:25:14,429
I’m here with you every step of the way.

411
00:25:18,475 --> 00:25:21,937
And you know where to find
me if you ever have a problem.

412
00:25:21,937 --> 00:25:23,355
In your room?

413
00:25:23,355 --> 00:25:25,482
Yeah. In my room.

414
00:25:27,359 --> 00:25:28,818
In my room.

415
00:25:32,739 --> 00:25:34,866
I’m so happy, Ke.

416
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:41,933
<i>Hello! I’m free tomorrow.</i>

417
00:26:44,519 --> 00:26:46,563
I’m Shan, nice to meet you.

418
00:26:46,563 --> 00:26:48,607
I’m hoping to get to know you more.

419
00:27:04,998 --> 00:27:11,087
Jeez, I already told you two, I’m just
going to beat you Juarez brothers at golf.

420
00:27:11,796 --> 00:27:14,507
Play polo with me. I swear I’ll beat you.

421
00:27:15,091 --> 00:27:16,384
Okay, let’s play tomorrow.

422
00:27:16,509 --> 00:27:16,885
Sure.

423
00:27:16,885 --> 00:27:17,761
Are you guys available?

424
00:27:17,761 --> 00:27:18,553
- Yeah.
- Let’s go.

425
00:27:18,553 --> 00:27:18,845
Okay.

426
00:27:18,845 --> 00:27:20,597
I’m just gonna beat you two again, though.

427
00:27:21,389 --> 00:27:22,307
We’ll see.

428
00:27:22,515 --> 00:27:23,642
We’ll see.

429
00:27:24,017 --> 00:27:26,561
Don’t get too cocky. You two don’t
stand a chance against me.

430
00:27:31,483 --> 00:27:34,110
<i>Okay. I’ll pick you up tomorrow.</i>

431
00:27:34,486 --> 00:27:35,695
<i>Just let me know what time.</i>

432
00:27:43,411 --> 00:27:44,579
Sorry.

433
00:27:44,996 --> 00:27:46,748
Turns out I’m not
free tomorrow after all.

434
00:27:47,499 --> 00:27:49,584
Why? Are you going somewhere?

435
00:28:12,774 --> 00:28:14,359
Are you okay?

436
00:28:18,321 --> 00:28:20,407
I’m seeing a new therapist.

437
00:28:21,241 --> 00:28:23,201
That’s good. How was it?

438
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:26,454
I don’t know.

439
00:28:27,205 --> 00:28:30,250
Not good, not bad.

440
00:28:31,167 --> 00:28:34,462
I’m starting to let out what
I’ve been holding in for so long.

441
00:28:35,547 --> 00:28:38,216
If only it could all come out in one go.

442
00:28:41,344 --> 00:28:43,221
Do you wanna talk about it?

443
00:28:43,972 --> 00:28:48,768
Or if you’d rather, we can
talk about something else.

444
00:28:48,768 --> 00:28:53,940
Do you know why I did what
I did the first time we met?

445
00:28:57,527 --> 00:29:02,782
Because I wanted to do
something I never used to do.

446
00:29:05,493 --> 00:29:07,078
I felt like a different person.

447
00:29:08,371 --> 00:29:10,290
<i>I wasn’t in pain.</i>

448
00:29:11,149 --> 00:29:12,459
<i>I wasn’t weak.</i>

449
00:29:15,003 --> 00:29:18,798
It was the first time I decided
to go out and live again.

450
00:29:24,053 --> 00:29:30,560
But before that, I thought about dying.

451
00:29:32,854 --> 00:29:33,688
A lot.

452
00:29:36,399 --> 00:29:38,485
Because I just wanted the pain to stop.

453
00:29:42,781 --> 00:29:45,784
The pain outside did go away,

454
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:48,244
but the pain inside feels like…

455
00:29:50,997 --> 00:29:53,666
something I’ll carry
for the rest of my life.

456
00:29:54,542 --> 00:30:00,653
Sometimes I’d go up somewhere high,
so I could see everything.

457
00:30:02,550 --> 00:30:03,747
No reason at all.

458
00:30:05,887 --> 00:30:06,888
It’s just pretty to look at.

459
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:09,974
It’s calming.

460
00:30:13,019 --> 00:30:15,004
It was the last thing I wanted to see.

461
00:30:17,982 --> 00:30:18,942
But?

462
00:30:20,026 --> 00:30:25,406
But Luna lost herself when
she thought she’d lost me.

463
00:30:28,451 --> 00:30:33,289
My parents love me so much.

464
00:30:33,794 --> 00:30:39,137
I wanted more time so I could give
back all the love they gave me.

465
00:30:41,351 --> 00:30:43,270
So that’s what you’re holding on to?

466
00:30:44,634 --> 00:30:46,469
I guess you and your
parents are close, huh?

467
00:30:49,138 --> 00:30:50,153
What about you?

468
00:31:01,192 --> 00:31:02,151
No.

469
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:06,656
I lost my mom when I was a kid.

470
00:31:08,825 --> 00:31:10,535
I only have my dad now.

471
00:31:11,369 --> 00:31:14,956
But I don’t see him as my father anymore.

472
00:31:15,905 --> 00:31:17,073
So I’m living alone.

473
00:31:21,408 --> 00:31:22,575
He’s...

474
00:31:26,092 --> 00:31:27,302
He’s violent.

475
00:31:28,636 --> 00:31:29,679
Since when?

476
00:31:30,513 --> 00:31:32,265
Honestly, I can’t remember.

477
00:31:33,674 --> 00:31:35,551
Four? Five?

478
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:38,813
Maybe even earlier.

479
00:31:39,772 --> 00:31:41,024
I’m sorry.

480
00:31:42,609 --> 00:31:43,443
Don’t be.

481
00:31:46,362 --> 00:31:48,072
He’s the one at fault for all of that.

482
00:31:51,784 --> 00:31:53,494
How do you face him?

483
00:31:55,322 --> 00:31:58,434
I’ve been holding
so much anger inside.

484
00:32:00,585 --> 00:32:03,254
So I’m not afraid to face him.

485
00:32:04,339 --> 00:32:08,343
And I keep telling myself he’s
the one who should be afraid of me.

486
00:32:10,219 --> 00:32:12,597
But it’s not always like that.

487
00:32:14,724 --> 00:32:21,981
So if there’s ever a chance I’ll never
have to face him again, I’d take it.

488
00:32:26,444 --> 00:32:27,772
I want to be like you.

489
00:32:29,447 --> 00:32:30,823
You’re so brave.

490
00:32:31,706 --> 00:32:33,374
You’re not afraid of anything.

491
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:35,995
Don’t.

492
00:32:37,121 --> 00:32:39,332
Ke, you’re a good person.

493
00:32:39,874 --> 00:32:41,709
And your heart is so pure.

494
00:32:43,795 --> 00:32:46,297
So if there’s anyone I want to be like—

495
00:32:48,132 --> 00:32:49,384
it’s you.

496
00:32:50,385 --> 00:32:54,973
If only I could see
myself the way you see me.

497
00:32:56,516 --> 00:32:59,268
Maybe I wouldn’t hate myself as much.

498
00:33:01,854 --> 00:33:07,360
By the way, didn’t you say you wanted
us to start over from the beginning?

499
00:33:08,778 --> 00:33:13,074
So here, I prepared some
topics we could explore.

500
00:33:16,421 --> 00:33:17,672
This is good.

501
00:33:18,908 --> 00:33:19,959
I’ll add some.

502
00:33:21,124 --> 00:33:24,669
Wait, what should we do on our next escape?

503
00:33:25,925 --> 00:33:28,052
You still want to blow off steam, right?

504
00:33:50,528 --> 00:33:51,112
Game?

505
00:33:59,328 --> 00:33:59,912
Yes!

506
00:34:36,199 --> 00:34:37,075
Nice!

507
00:34:37,909 --> 00:34:41,621
<i>I didn’t think it was possible to let</i>
<i>out frustration without fear or anger.</i>

508
00:34:42,663 --> 00:34:43,539
<i>Yeah.</i>

509
00:35:12,318 --> 00:35:14,737
You said you and
your dad are close.

510
00:35:15,279 --> 00:35:15,947
Yup.

511
00:35:17,031 --> 00:35:19,200
I have a good relationship with my dad.

512
00:35:19,617 --> 00:35:24,580
That’s why I love art, because we like
to spend a lot of time making art together.

513
00:35:25,373 --> 00:35:27,583
My first painting was even framed.

514
00:35:29,669 --> 00:35:31,129
Your dad’s so cool, huh?

515
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:35,758
You know what, I want to see everything
you two have made, all your artworks.

516
00:35:35,758 --> 00:35:38,511
Dad has an art room at home.

517
00:35:39,053 --> 00:35:41,623
It’s a little messy,
since there’s paint and

518
00:35:41,647 --> 00:35:44,517
canvases everywhere,
but it’s a beautiful mess.

519
00:35:44,976 --> 00:35:46,477
But, you should come and see it.

520
00:35:46,811 --> 00:35:48,396
Yeah, I’d love to.

521
00:35:50,690 --> 00:35:53,151
I already know what we should do next.

522
00:36:02,451 --> 00:36:04,120
How was your childhood?

523
00:36:06,414 --> 00:36:08,416
I was cheerful as a kid.

524
00:36:08,666 --> 00:36:10,459
I was always with Luna.

525
00:36:10,918 --> 00:36:15,006
Dad’s from Bataan, so we
always went there for vacation.

526
00:36:15,673 --> 00:36:19,010
Especially by the sea.

527
00:36:21,262 --> 00:36:22,889
I like making new friends.

528
00:36:23,556 --> 00:36:25,808
I feel like a different
person when I’m there.

529
00:36:26,058 --> 00:36:27,810
They call me by a different name there.

530
00:36:28,519 --> 00:36:29,312
What do they call you?

531
00:36:29,562 --> 00:36:30,354
Ayi.

532
00:36:30,730 --> 00:36:31,731
Ayi?

533
00:36:32,815 --> 00:36:35,109
I couldn’t say my name back then.

534
00:36:35,109 --> 00:36:38,863
So it became “Zayin.”
Eventually it became “Ayi”.

535
00:36:39,906 --> 00:36:41,657
You’re from Bataan too, right?

536
00:36:42,033 --> 00:36:43,117
Yes, I am.

537
00:36:49,999 --> 00:36:51,459
Why are you looking at me like that?

538
00:36:54,086 --> 00:36:55,129
No reason.

539
00:36:55,963 --> 00:36:57,506
I want to see your childhood photos.

540
00:36:58,633 --> 00:37:00,760
At home. We have some at home.

541
00:37:00,760 --> 00:37:02,595
What about you?
Do you have photos?

542
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:04,513
Yeah.

543
00:37:04,764 --> 00:37:07,683
But the only photos I kept
are the ones with my mom.

544
00:37:07,767 --> 00:37:08,726
Let me see.

545
00:37:09,393 --> 00:37:09,943
Sure.

546
00:38:11,455 --> 00:38:12,415
I’m done!

547
00:38:12,790 --> 00:38:13,916
Exchange?

548
00:38:14,750 --> 00:38:17,044
Wait, wait. Just a little, just a little.

549
00:38:17,545 --> 00:38:19,046
Let me finish this.

550
00:38:20,881 --> 00:38:21,841
Okay. There.

551
00:38:22,008 --> 00:38:23,134
- Ready?
- Okay?

552
00:38:24,010 --> 00:38:25,219
Mine first.

553
00:38:25,511 --> 00:38:26,178
Yours first?

554
00:38:26,178 --> 00:38:26,929
Mhmm.

555
00:38:33,686 --> 00:38:34,645
You go first.

556
00:38:39,025 --> 00:38:39,900
Wow.

557
00:38:40,609 --> 00:38:41,986
This one’s really pretty.

558
00:38:42,695 --> 00:38:43,654
Thank you.

559
00:38:44,113 --> 00:38:45,323
You’re really good.

560
00:38:46,198 --> 00:38:47,325
Can I look now?

561
00:38:50,369 --> 00:38:51,412
Maybe not…

562
00:38:51,537 --> 00:38:52,163
Huh?

563
00:38:52,163 --> 00:38:52,621
Forget it.

564
00:38:52,621 --> 00:38:54,290
Come on. I thought it was okay?

565
00:38:54,749 --> 00:38:55,541
Let me fix it a bit more.

566
00:38:55,875 --> 00:38:57,168
It’s fine!

567
00:38:57,460 --> 00:38:58,268
Okay?

568
00:38:58,753 --> 00:38:59,712
I’m gonna look at it now.

569
00:39:00,796 --> 00:39:01,547
Okay.

570
00:39:03,841 --> 00:39:05,343
Hey, I like this.

571
00:39:05,885 --> 00:39:09,764
Can I keep it? Dad’s the only
one who’s ever painted me.

572
00:39:10,431 --> 00:39:11,474
Are you sure?

573
00:39:12,391 --> 00:39:14,560
It’s not as pretty as this one, though.

574
00:39:14,685 --> 00:39:16,562
Come on, it’s really pretty.

575
00:39:17,938 --> 00:39:19,440
Is this how you see me?

576
00:39:26,113 --> 00:39:27,281
You’re even prettier than that.

577
00:39:39,710 --> 00:39:40,711
Thanks, Lawrence.

578
00:39:40,711 --> 00:39:41,754
- You’re the best. Thanks.
- Sure thing, ma’am.

579
00:39:41,754 --> 00:39:42,588
Thank you.

580
00:39:45,545 --> 00:39:48,677
Our topic is “places
important to us,” right?

581
00:39:51,263 --> 00:39:53,224
Welcome to Valeria High!

582
00:39:54,775 --> 00:39:58,320
But you haven’t even told me
why this place matters to you.

583
00:39:58,437 --> 00:39:59,688
This is where I went to high school.

584
00:40:01,065 --> 00:40:01,982
Really?

585
00:40:03,377 --> 00:40:04,795
What the hell is happening?

586
00:40:05,111 --> 00:40:07,071
What’s wrong?
Is there a problem?

587
00:40:07,281 --> 00:40:09,826
Why do you look like
you’ve seen a ghost?

588
00:40:11,075 --> 00:40:12,243
Come on, let’s go.

589
00:40:21,961 --> 00:40:23,796
We do the events here sometimes.

590
00:40:24,130 --> 00:40:27,967
Foundation Day is my favorite
because other schools can come visit.

591
00:40:31,053 --> 00:40:31,929
I know.

592
00:40:33,180 --> 00:40:35,516
Actually, I know there
were a bunch of booths here.

593
00:40:35,766 --> 00:40:39,520
There was also a booth where you can win
stuffed toys. There’s a cafe too, right?

594
00:40:40,485 --> 00:40:41,730
How do you know that?

595
00:40:41,730 --> 00:40:43,065
Wait, where did you
go to high school again?

596
00:40:43,607 --> 00:40:44,525
Lopez High.

597
00:40:44,692 --> 00:40:45,818
Lopez High…

598
00:40:46,907 --> 00:40:47,903
Are you sure?

599
00:40:48,529 --> 00:40:49,238
I’ll walk you out.

600
00:40:49,238 --> 00:40:50,865
All right, fine. I’ll be back.

601
00:40:50,990 --> 00:40:51,740
You sure?

602
00:40:52,324 --> 00:40:53,117
Hi, Pres!

603
00:40:57,079 --> 00:40:58,164
Aren’t you guys gonna look around?

604
00:40:59,665 --> 00:41:03,294
Oh right, how could I forget?

605
00:41:04,211 --> 00:41:05,421
We’ve met before.

606
00:41:05,546 --> 00:41:06,505
Huh? Where?

607
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:08,424
Here. Right here.

608
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:10,843
You greeted Acel.

609
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:11,969
You know him, right?

610
00:41:11,969 --> 00:41:13,846
Pres? He’s your friend?

611
00:41:14,263 --> 00:41:15,973
Wow, small world.

612
00:41:15,973 --> 00:41:17,475
But how come I don’t remember you?

613
00:41:19,268 --> 00:41:20,394
How about now?

614
00:41:23,564 --> 00:41:24,648
Nothing?

615
00:41:24,648 --> 00:41:25,357
How about this?

616
00:41:27,151 --> 00:41:28,027
No—

617
00:41:28,027 --> 00:41:29,153
You don’t remember?

618
00:41:29,695 --> 00:41:32,364
We came here before.
I remember it clearly.

619
00:41:34,950 --> 00:41:36,869
I really don’t remember.

620
00:41:37,119 --> 00:41:39,079
But why were you
looking at me like that?

621
00:41:40,331 --> 00:41:43,083
Because you looked familiar.
I just couldn’t remember.

622
00:41:44,084 --> 00:41:45,169
Isn’t that something?

623
00:41:45,336 --> 00:41:49,256
The world is so big, yet we keep
finding ourselves in the same places.

624
00:41:49,924 --> 00:41:53,135
Maybe there’s a reason we keep
running into each other, even back then.

625
00:41:54,470 --> 00:41:55,429
You think so?

626
00:41:56,847 --> 00:42:00,726
Do you think this will keep happening
to us even when we’re old?

627
00:42:00,935 --> 00:42:02,186
Maybe.

628
00:42:03,020 --> 00:42:03,812
Probably.

629
00:42:05,105 --> 00:42:06,023
I hope so.

630
00:42:07,024 --> 00:42:08,901
Only time will tell.

631
00:43:01,245 --> 00:43:03,247
Can’t you see I’m having a moment here?

632
00:43:07,334 --> 00:43:12,047
By the way, this is where our
high school friend group was formed.

633
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:13,591
How many of you are there?

634
00:43:15,050 --> 00:43:20,556
Luna, Sam, Yanna, Via, Arkin, and Sevi.

635
00:43:22,683 --> 00:43:26,645
High school was one of the
best times of my life, if not the best.

636
00:43:28,272 --> 00:43:32,526
Every time I come back here,
it’s like a time machine.

637
00:43:33,235 --> 00:43:35,029
It takes me back to how happy we were.

638
00:43:35,446 --> 00:43:38,657
Now we hardly get to
hang out together anymore.

639
00:43:39,992 --> 00:43:41,201
Same here.

640
00:43:41,827 --> 00:43:45,664
That’s why I get you.
We’re drifting apart, too.

641
00:43:45,664 --> 00:43:50,836
If only we could go back, right?
Just be happy all the time.

642
00:43:54,715 --> 00:43:58,260
Let’s start making your
yesterdays happy, starting today.

643
00:44:20,282 --> 00:44:21,784
Thanks for today.

644
00:44:23,202 --> 00:44:24,620
Thank you, too, for today.

645
00:44:24,912 --> 00:44:26,830
I really enjoyed everything we did.

646
00:44:27,539 --> 00:44:28,832
Are there still a lot on the list?

647
00:44:29,416 --> 00:44:30,542
Yes, a lot.

648
00:44:30,793 --> 00:44:34,546
So hopefully, when you’re free,
we can get to them right away.

649
00:44:38,842 --> 00:44:39,551
Ke.

650
00:44:41,220 --> 00:44:42,471
Good night.

651
00:44:43,013 --> 00:44:44,723
And see you yesterday.

652
00:44:45,557 --> 00:44:47,059
See you yesterday.

653
00:45:11,959 --> 00:45:13,794
Why are you smiling like that?

654
00:45:13,794 --> 00:45:15,045
What’s up?

655
00:45:17,516 --> 00:45:19,434
Is there something that’s making you happy?

656
00:45:21,385 --> 00:45:22,136
Or…

657
00:45:22,302 --> 00:45:23,887
Or is it someone?

658
00:45:24,513 --> 00:45:28,767
Is it someone? What about you?
Is it someone? Do you have a boyfriend?

659
00:45:29,518 --> 00:45:33,021
Huh, me? You know me.
I’m busy with my studies.

660
00:45:33,313 --> 00:45:35,524
Also, I’m busy with cheer dancing.

661
00:45:37,401 --> 00:45:39,027
Don’t change the subject, Shan.

662
00:45:39,027 --> 00:45:40,904
Why are you smiling like that?

663
00:45:42,072 --> 00:45:43,991
I’m just happy with my coffee.

664
00:45:44,491 --> 00:45:48,662
So don’t change the subject either,
or do you want me to ask Roel instead?

665
00:45:49,788 --> 00:45:52,541
Shan, can you make me
a coffee too, please? Three shots.

666
00:45:52,541 --> 00:45:55,294
Bathroom... I’m just going to
the bathroom first, okay? Thank you.

667
00:46:06,722 --> 00:46:07,723
How are you?

668
00:46:09,308 --> 00:46:13,479
Stressed and distracted because of school.

669
00:46:15,022 --> 00:46:18,192
But there are fewer nightmares now,

670
00:46:18,192 --> 00:46:21,570
since I’m not sleeping much
with all the work I have.

671
00:46:22,988 --> 00:46:26,867
But I can say I feel...

672
00:46:27,618 --> 00:46:29,703
I don’t feel worse than before.

673
00:46:30,788 --> 00:46:31,789
That’s good.

674
00:46:32,748 --> 00:46:35,375
But sleep is a priority, okay?

675
00:46:36,835 --> 00:46:38,629
Take a break when you can.

676
00:46:40,672 --> 00:46:45,260
How about going out?
Any progress?

677
00:46:47,346 --> 00:46:51,517
I went to a place that’s
important to me, and—

678
00:46:54,603 --> 00:46:57,523
Before the incident.

679
00:46:58,232 --> 00:47:03,570
I was happy because I
remembered my old self.

680
00:47:04,472 --> 00:47:09,436
The high school Kierra,
bright and innocent.

681
00:47:15,541 --> 00:47:19,169
But I also felt bad because...

682
00:47:20,796 --> 00:47:25,843
I remembered the future that
high school Kierra would face.

683
00:47:35,102 --> 00:47:36,728
I betrayed that kid.

684
00:47:37,855 --> 00:47:39,106
No.

685
00:47:40,023 --> 00:47:41,984
You did not betray her.

686
00:47:42,568 --> 00:47:44,695
You did not betray yourself.

687
00:47:45,445 --> 00:47:49,032
In fact, despite what you went through—

688
00:47:49,950 --> 00:47:55,455
you’re still the loving person that you
are, and you extend that love to others.

689
00:47:57,840 --> 00:48:00,467
You did not betray yourself, Kierra.

690
00:48:01,837 --> 00:48:03,338
He betrayed you.

691
00:48:11,346 --> 00:48:15,726
Doc, I’m ready to continue.

692
00:48:37,372 --> 00:48:40,000
Can you just leave me alone, Miguel?
I haven’t slept yet.

693
00:48:40,000 --> 00:48:42,920
I just want to know one thing, bro.
What do you know about me?

694
00:48:42,920 --> 00:48:44,296
What are you so afraid of?

695
00:48:46,089 --> 00:48:48,717
You mentioned Kierra. Why?

696
00:48:50,260 --> 00:48:53,597
So you do know her.
Why did you pretend you didn’t?

697
00:48:53,973 --> 00:48:55,950
I didn’t pretend. I didn’t pretend.

698
00:48:57,019 --> 00:48:58,521
She’s just not…

699
00:48:59,186 --> 00:49:01,396
that important for me to remember her.

700
00:49:02,981 --> 00:49:06,735
Why? Is she saying something?
Is she talking to people?

701
00:49:06,944 --> 00:49:11,031
Dude, if I were you, I’d stay
away from her, you know why?

702
00:49:11,698 --> 00:49:13,200
She’s a little crazy.

703
00:49:13,533 --> 00:49:14,785
Shut up.

704
00:49:15,535 --> 00:49:17,537
Unless something’s going
on between you two?

705
00:49:17,537 --> 00:49:18,716
Is there?

706
00:49:18,747 --> 00:49:22,042
‘Cause dude, I’m telling you,
she almost ruined my life.

707
00:49:22,042 --> 00:49:25,504
She would spread rumors about me.
She could do that to you.

708
00:49:25,504 --> 00:49:26,964
You want to be a lawyer, right?

709
00:49:26,964 --> 00:49:29,007
What if your reputation gets
ruined? ​​Then think about me.

710
00:49:29,007 --> 00:49:30,467
You know she sleeps
around, she sleeps around.

711
00:49:30,467 --> 00:49:32,803
She’d do anything, I’m telling you.

712
00:49:32,803 --> 00:49:34,930
Absolutely anything just
to get what she wants.

713
00:49:34,930 --> 00:49:35,931
She’s sick in the head.

714
00:49:35,931 --> 00:49:37,766
I heard she’s seeing a doctor.

715
00:49:37,766 --> 00:49:39,810
And who does that? Sick people.

716
00:49:39,810 --> 00:49:40,644
Like Kierra.

717
00:49:40,644 --> 00:49:42,104
She’s pretty, but she’s crazy.

718
00:49:42,437 --> 00:49:43,188
Dude, she’s kind of crazy—

719
00:49:43,188 --> 00:49:44,731
I said shut up!

720
00:50:29,276 --> 00:50:32,320
Have you thought about
where we’ll go next?

721
00:50:32,946 --> 00:50:34,906
Places important to you, I mean.

722
00:50:34,906 --> 00:50:36,950
Yes. Whenever you’re free again.

723
00:50:36,950 --> 00:50:37,951
Where?

724
00:50:38,991 --> 00:50:40,368
You should say hi to Mom.

725
00:50:41,794 --> 00:50:44,129
I’m not ready to cross
over to the afterlife yet.

726
00:50:44,541 --> 00:50:45,500
You’re scaring me.

727
00:50:45,500 --> 00:50:47,335
I know. I meant the cemetery.

728
00:50:47,878 --> 00:50:49,796
I’m sure she’d love to see you again.

729
00:50:50,255 --> 00:50:52,674
She was so fond of
you when you were little.

730
00:50:54,134 --> 00:50:56,845
We really did meet before in Bataan.

731
00:50:57,137 --> 00:50:59,431
You’re the kid with all those
different colored hair clips.

732
00:51:02,184 --> 00:51:04,686
Oh, your sandcastle is so pretty!

733
00:51:06,229 --> 00:51:08,482
I'm Ayi. That's my nickname.

734
00:51:22,537 --> 00:51:23,789
Who are you?

735
00:51:30,420 --> 00:51:31,671
You're here again.

736
00:51:31,671 --> 00:51:33,882
I wonder why we keep
running into each other.

737
00:51:33,882 --> 00:51:36,134
What do you think? Destiny?

738
00:51:36,593 --> 00:51:39,596
If you were to ask me, maybe
we should start from the top?

739
00:51:39,653 --> 00:51:41,655
I’m Shan. Nice to meet you.

740
00:51:42,140 --> 00:51:43,124
Hello! I’m Kierra.

741
00:51:51,399 --> 00:51:52,484
Is that a bruise?

742
00:51:52,901 --> 00:51:53,902
What happened?

743
00:51:55,654 --> 00:51:57,030
Are you sure you’re okay?

744
00:51:57,906 --> 00:52:00,283
Do you want to stay at our
condo with Luna for a while?

745
00:52:04,663 --> 00:52:05,914
Hi, Luna.

746
00:52:06,224 --> 00:52:07,642
Don’t you “hi, Luna” me.

747
00:52:07,999 --> 00:52:09,543
Are you hungry? I’ll cook for you.

748
00:52:09,543 --> 00:52:10,919
I can cook, is that okay?

749
00:52:11,044 --> 00:52:13,588
Huh? You’re not allowed to use our kitchen.

750
00:52:13,588 --> 00:52:15,382
Can you two please not fight?

751
00:52:15,382 --> 00:52:17,926
You’re such a jerk, Shondei.

752
00:52:19,094 --> 00:52:22,139
You know, Luna, he still loves you.

753
00:52:22,139 --> 00:52:23,181
For you.

754
00:52:25,058 --> 00:52:26,184
You’re together now?

755
00:52:26,726 --> 00:52:28,395
Didn’t she kiss you before?

756
00:52:29,229 --> 00:52:31,690
Welcome to the Bataan house.

757
00:52:35,927 --> 00:52:38,155
- One, two, three.
- Smile!

758
00:52:39,406 --> 00:52:40,365
So sweet!

759
00:52:40,699 --> 00:52:41,783
Merry Christmas.

760
00:52:42,117 --> 00:52:43,535
Thank you for bringing me here.

761
00:52:46,413 --> 00:52:47,956
- Don’t be shy now.
- Ke.
